From: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 22:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: keep MAC-to-PHY XFI flow control off on
 the PON PCS

XFI GIB flow control is enabled towards the PHY in two places: an
unconditional set in airoha_pcs_post_config(), and a rewrite in
airoha_pcs_config() driven by permit_pause_to_mac (which phylink keeps
enabled by default). phylink_major_config() invokes pcs_post_config()
before pcs_config(), so the config-time write is the one that sticks
and both write sites have to be changed.

The MAC-to-PHY direction (XFI_TX_FC_EN) asserts backpressure towards
the attached PHY when the fabric side is congested, e.g. by
hardware-offloaded flows whose egress port is saturated. A
rate-adapting copper PHY cannot relieve this backpressure when the
copper link partner does not honour pause frames: the RTL8261N's
USXGMII side wedges and the PHY drops and retrains the copper link,
causing a multi-second link loss.

Keep XFI_TX_FC_EN disabled for the PON PCS variant in both write sites
so that congestion is dropped in the fabric instead of stalling the
PHY. XFI_RX_FC_EN (the PHY pacing the MAC, required for rate
adaptation) stays enabled.

Signed-off-by: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
---
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
@@ -700,7 +700,10 @@
 	regmap_update_bits(maps->pcs_mac, AIROHA_PCS_XFI_MAC_XFI_GIB_CFG,
 			   AIROHA_PCS_XFI_TX_FC_EN | AIROHA_PCS_XFI_RX_FC_EN,
 			   permit_pause_to_mac ?
-				AIROHA_PCS_XFI_TX_FC_EN | AIROHA_PCS_XFI_RX_FC_EN :
+				(priv->data->port_type == AIROHA_PCS_PON ?
+					AIROHA_PCS_XFI_RX_FC_EN :
+					AIROHA_PCS_XFI_TX_FC_EN |
+					AIROHA_PCS_XFI_RX_FC_EN) :
 				0);

 	return 0;
@@ -960,8 +963,10 @@
 			   FIELD_PREP(AIROHA_PCS_XFI_IPG_NUM, 10));

 	/* Enable TX/RX flow control */
-	regmap_set_bits(maps->pcs_mac, AIROHA_PCS_XFI_MAC_XFI_GIB_CFG,
-			AIROHA_PCS_XFI_TX_FC_EN);
+	regmap_update_bits(maps->pcs_mac, AIROHA_PCS_XFI_MAC_XFI_GIB_CFG,
+			   AIROHA_PCS_XFI_TX_FC_EN,
+			   priv->data->port_type == AIROHA_PCS_PON ?
+				0 : AIROHA_PCS_XFI_TX_FC_EN);
 	regmap_set_bits(maps->pcs_mac, AIROHA_PCS_XFI_MAC_XFI_GIB_CFG,
 			AIROHA_PCS_XFI_RX_FC_EN);

